  "name": "Citizens versus Ravels - the ruined middle",
  "notes": "The first asymmetric fixture, on the default 48x16 preset - the one the whole composition is derived from, so the Grid fills the viewport exactly. Ten Citizens against eleven Ravels, each in front of a Grid Nexus: fewer and tougher on one cadence against more, faster, off the beat, and mostly explosive. Neither roster is a Commander Army; both are disposable bench content, and the point is contrast rather than balance. Both sides are staggered across columns on purpose - with every unit on one rank an entire army targets one enemy, because at long range every enemy is equidistant in Chebyshev and the tie breaks on entity id (Q17).",
